android: route joystick motion through the text-input view

While text input is on, SDL's DummyEdit holds focus, so Android delivers
generic motion events (gamepad sticks and triggers) to it instead of the
SDLSurface that carries SDL's motion listener. Buttons still arrive through its
key listener, so a stick released while the view has focus never reports its
return to centre and its direction sticks.

--- a/android-project/app/src/main/java/org/libsdl/app/SDLActivity.java
+++ b/android-project/app/src/main/java/org/libsdl/app/SDLActivity.java
@@ -1902,6 +1902,8 @@
         setFocusableInTouchMode(true);
         setFocusable(true);
         setOnKeyListener(this);
+        // Focused while text input is on, so joystick motion lands here.
+        setOnGenericMotionListener(SDLActivity.getMotionListener());
     }
 
     @Override
